{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact JP1 head 1e2dae29124e8d75d0bdf2a85d3cc212c8acb09e on builder/join-parity-jp1-20261110, all 19 artifacts, for request 3c9a0f81 under promise 89e47999 and review request 21810ee7. The head does what 3c9a0f81 asks. Start, the CLI and MCP read a person link with one parser, require its explicit Membership pin, and accept a terminal slash on its service.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `invitationOf` (`packages/client/src/invitation.ts`) is the one parser. It refuses a link with no `definition` or no string `service`, strips terminal slashes from the service, refuses an empty service, and compares against an expected service when the caller gives one. `InvitationLink.definition` is now required. `wellFormedInvitation` also requires `isInvitationMembership(link.definition)`.\n- The CLI copy in `browser-helpers.ts` is gone. `linkOf`, `LINK` and `Link` stay as re-exports of the client names, so the public export at client `index.ts` and its CLI callers keep working. `browser-joining.ts` passes `context.origin` as the expected service.\n- Item 2. The `platform:membership@1` fallback is gone from `command-membership.ts` and from MCP `#join`. I found no other person-link fallback at the head. `invitations.ts:73` defaults agent-key rows to `@2`, which is a different link kind. Both person-link writers, `dap invite` (`command-membership.ts:43`) and the retained issue (`invitations.ts:362`), already write the pin.\n- Item 3. Page passes `session.service`, the CLI passes the saved config's service, and MCP passes `this.#service || undefined`. A fresh CLI or an empty MCP server learns the normalized service from the link. MCP no longer compares raw strings.\n- Item 4. The head adds no tagged receiver and no check mode.\n- The CLI join now reads the config before it parses the link, and it refuses a link for another service before it reads any key or private request. Submission and settlement use a `ScopeHandle` with no signer. The signed-read handle exists only after acceptance, so a pending join reads the key once. That repair fixed the first focus failure, and the original assertion stays.\n- A pending join that an earlier build saved with a slash in its service stays retained and fails comparison. The CLI witness shows no send, no key read, no private read and no write in that case. The note and `docs/cli.md` say so.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main af3badef is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 19 paths that the 19 artifacts cover, and the primary artifact is neither stale nor retired. From b614c87d to the head, only the note and its evidence manifest change.\n- Cheap checks. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The commit-message check passes: 8 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean.\n- Tests, on my own extracted copy, with no shared validation slot. `packages/cli/test/invitation-link.test.ts` and `packages/mcp/test/errors.test.ts` pass 19 of 19. Those two files carry the shared six-row table for the CLI and MCP. The Page rows run in `apps/room/page/test/join.test.ts`, which I read and did not run.\n- Evidence. The 30 files that the manifest lists match their SHA-256 values in `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-12-jp1-b614-final-public-8726d6cf`. `SHA256SUMS` verifies, and `manifest.json` hashes to `88ed2aaa…0b20`, as the note says. The gate counts agree with END 80d96e43: 5,900 selected cases, 5,897 passes and three planned skips.\n- CI. GitHub reports Page run 43162619378 and Card run 43162622935 as push events, attempt 1, completed and successful, at the head.\n\nThe Page control, under ruling cd42bc3d. I accept it as a distinguishing control. The failed unit records one Page child that exited 1 with two cases: one passed and one failed. The failure is at `join.test.ts:55:53`, \"promise resolved instead of rejecting\". At the head, line 55 is the `rejects.toThrow` loop over changed links, and that loop includes `{ ...original, definition: undefined }`. With the `@1` fallback restored, the missing-pin link resolves, so the intended assertion goes red. Controller 963 still failed, with exit 2, because its classifier expected different words. That failure belongs to the harness, not to the head. The MCP-only control failed at its named assertion, `errors.test.ts:442:35`, with 17 other cases passing.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One parser in `packages/client` owns the person-link rules, and each surface supplies only its expected service. JP2's tagged agent invitation and check mode keep their place.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Each surface refuses a missing pin and another service before signing, before reading a key and before writing custody. The witnesses count those reads and writes. An old pending join with a slash fails closed: the CLI sends nothing and signs no replacement. The head changes no saved request, historical link or original signature.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes for a later head:\n\n1. A service mismatch now gives a less specific reason. MCP returns the `shape` error for `link` instead of the old `target` error that named both services. The CLI says \"not an invitation link from dap invite, or it names another service\". The browser says \"That is not an invitation link.\" instead of \"This invitation is for another service.\" The parser could say which check refused the link.\n2. The browser compares strings after `invitationOf` strips slashes, while `offered` still parses URLs. A link whose service names the same origin in a different form, with an explicit `:443` port for example, now fails in the parser. No dap writer emits that form.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing, export or deployment. The planner decides the landing. The snapshot export stays pending for Hugh, as fc580b1a says.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bdff5b9c6e610e51f1cb150ec265e50298b9c218"